# Plans must include /simplify-pr and /no-comments

Whenever you create or revise an implementation plan for this project (Plan mode, `/plan`, or any written plan before coding):

- Include explicit late steps to run `/simplify-pr` then `/no-comments` on the plan's scoped diff (caller files/diff, otherwise the branch/working-tree diff against `main`).
- Do not mark the plan complete, or claim implementation done, until both steps have been executed per `.agents/skills/simplify-pr/SKILL.md` and `.agents/skills/no-comments/SKILL.md`.
- Keep both in scope for code-changing plans; skip them only for pure docs/tooling plans that touch no application source under `src/`.
- Order: implement → verify as required → `/simplify-pr` (apply in-scope cuts) → `/no-comments` (last).
